    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I haven&#39;t tried running your code, but I think the problem is that you&#39;re not backtick-ing the `data-toggle` and `data-target` attributes.  It&#39;s not a shiny problem, it just has to do with legal names in R. Using a dash inside a name is &quot;not valid&quot; so you need to surround it with backticks.  Same reason as why you can&#39;t run <div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#008\">my</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#008\">var</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></font></div></code></div>but you can create a similar variable by surrounding it with backticks</div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#080\">`my-var`</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span></font></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
